pleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nVersion v4.5.stable.official [876b29033] (or any version probably)\n\nHello! I appear to have encountered a bug. To reproduce the bug, the steps are simple.\n\nI have tested all major versions of Godot, and was able to reproduce it in every version. Although the code was different, the result appears to be the same. I have included a zip file containing example projects with all versions I tested. I think that the 1.0 version could provide the clearest insight into what is happening, since it does not use reload_current_scene yet still produces the same results.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7216) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400F @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.80 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n## Expected behavior:\nWhen the scene reloads, a child sprite3d retains the modulate of its parent sprite3d\n## Actual behavior:\nWhen the scene reloads, a child sprite3d ignores its parent modulate, setting instead to its own personal modulate\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create a new 3D/spatial scene with a sprite3d contained within.\n2. add another sprite3d as a child of the first sprite3d\n3. change the modulate on the first sprite3d\n4. attach a script that reloads the scene in code (easily done with input.is_action_pressed)\n5. ensure both sprites are visible, and set a camera to observe them\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[sp-3d-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23435361/sp-3d-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/a